'''Olga''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that could be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Merc Storia Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 2.2 Update#Version 2.2.9 Update|Version 2.2.9]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 112
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Olga
|name2 = Olga CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Olga CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Practically being a copy-paste of [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] means that Olga and he can be used interchangeably—not half bad for a measly collab rare. Using both of them simultaneously can prove effective in Red-dominant early-game stages, an example being [[Last Gang]] where [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] can be stun-locked twice as hard as he would against Pirate normally. As with Pirate, Olga can also help push back melee Red enemies such as [[Bore]].

This fair playing ground is discarded when the player is able to evolve Pirate into Dread Pirate Catley, who gains significant defensive buffs on top of a slightly higher proc chance through stat increases and [[Talents]]. Olga, unable to receive such buffs, is reduced to situational support for Catley, though he usually does his job well enough to not need it. Stages with [[Wave Attack]]s completely ditch the idea of using Olga, as only Catley is able to have [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]]. Olga's only prominent use from there on is in [[Merciless Onslaught]], where low-damage, Red-knockback units are key to defeat the stage.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Midranger}}

